From c85362407b15c539c4ab772a21b6e6f8c2d73291 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TennyWang1223 <Tenny.Wang@amd.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 10:23:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] WIP: gfx1250 Lamport AR+RMSNorm speedups vs PR #8022 Gluon
 (experimental)

Local checkpoint, not for review. On top of PR #8022 head 1aef2c832.
- peer pointers as scalar kernargs (full kernarg preload, static indices)
- row mode: PACKS packs a thread; LDS-only barrier (no wait on remote
  store acks); DPP/permlanex16 wave butterfly; one-barrier row fold
- fp contract(off) to keep car_fused bit-exactness with PACKS > 1
- SPLIT mode: sender blocks (+ re-arm) and one receiver block a row,
  tx/rx round counters (AR+add / AG also write rx)
- poll the ngpus-1 peer slots only
- experimental: cluster with sender waves that exit (slower, to revert)
- TEMP env knobs: AITER_LAMPORT_RMS_{CLUSTER,PACKS,CBS,SPLIT,SENDPACKS,LDS};
  LAMPORT_STAMPS timing macro (off)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
